{"timestamp":"2026-04-22T22:11:14.856Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"I found the root cause.\n\nThe failing E2E repo is configured for `checkpoints_version: 2`, but its installed git hook script is:\n\n```sh\nentire hooks git post-commit\n```\n\nThat matters because in E2E:\n- normal CLI calls use `E2E_ENTIRE_BIN=/tmp/entire-e2e`\n- but git hooks do not use `E2E_ENTIRE_BIN`\n- they invoke plain `entire` from `PATH`\n\nIn our focused runs, `PATH` only had:\n- `/tmp/vogon`\n- `/tmp/entire-e2e`\n\nThere was no `/tmp/entire`.\n\nSo the git hook was picking up some other `entire` binary from the machine, not the test binary we built for this branch. That explains the preserved repo exactly:\n- `.entire/settings.json` says `checkpoints_version: 2`\n- but the hook wrote only `refs/heads/entire/checkpoints/v1`\n- and `entire.log` showed `write_committed_v1_ms > 0`, `write_committed_v2_ms = 0`\n\nSo this is not a checkpoints-v2 logic bug. It is an E2E hook-binary selection bug.\n\nThe right fix is in E2E setup, not in checkpoint code. We need the hooks installed in E2E repos to point at the same binary as `E2E_ENTIRE_BIN`, either by:\n1. installing hooks with an absolute binary path, or\n2. adding a stable `entire` shim/symlink in PATH that points to `E2E_ENTIRE_BIN`\n\nI recommend option 1 if the CLI/setup path already supports absolute hook paths cleanly. Otherwise option 2 is a smaller E2E-only fix.\n\nIf you want, I’ll make that fix next as one step and rerun the focused Vogon attach tests in `v2-only`.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
