wrapper (enable, rewind, etc.)\n    28\t├── exploratory/  # Experimental tests, not run by CI\n    29\t├── tests/        # Blessed test files (run by CI)\n    30\t└── testutil/     # Repo setup, assertions, artifact capture\n    31\t```\n    32\t\n    33\t## Key Patterns\n    34\t\n    35\t- Every test uses `testutil.ForEachAgent` which runs it per registered agent with repo setup, concurrency gating, and timeout scaling.\n    36\t- All operations go through `RepoState` (`s.RunPrompt`, `s.Git`) so they're logged to `console.log`.\n    37\t- Use the `entire` package for CLI interactions, not raw `exec.Command`.\n    38\t- Skip tests pending CLI fixes with `t.Skip(\"ENT-XXX: reason\")`.\n    39\t\n    40\t## Adding a New Agent\n    41\t\n    42\t1. Create `agents/<name>.go` implementing the `Agent` interface.\n    43\t2. Register it in `init()` with `Register(&YourAgent{})`.\n    44\t3. Add a `Bootstrap()` method for any CI-specific setup (auth config, warmup).\n    45\t4. Add a `RegisterGate(\"<name>\", N)` call if concurrency needs limiting.\n    46\t5. Ensure the agent name is accepted by `mise run test:e2e --agent <name>`.\n    47\t6. Add the agent to `.github/workflows/e2e.yml` matrix and `e2e-isolated.yml` options.\n    48\t\n    49\t## Environment Variables\n    50\t\n    51\t| Variable | Description | Default |\n    52\t|----------|-------------|---------|\n    53\t| `E2E_AGENT` | Agent to test (`claude-code`, `gemini-cli`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `factoryai-droid`, `copilot-cli`) | all registered |\n    54\t| `E2E_ENTIRE_BIN` | Path to a pre-built `entire` binary | builds from source |\n    55\t| `E2E_TIMEOUT` | Timeout per prompt | `2m` |\n    56\t| `E2E_KEEP_REPOS` | Set to `1` to preserve temp repos after test | unset |\n    57\t| `E2E_ARTIFACT_DIR` | Override artifact output directory | `e2e/artifacts/<timestamp>` |\n    58\t| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | Required for Claude Code | — |\n    59\t| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | Required for Gemini CLI | — |\n    60\t| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | Required for Codex | — |\n    61\t| `COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN` | Required for Copilot CLI (or `gh auth login`) | — |\n    62\t\n    63\t## Debugging Failures\n    64\t\n    65\tArtifacts are captured to `e2e/artifacts/` on every run (git-log, git-tree, console.log, checkpoint metadata, entire logs). Set `E2E_KEEP_REPOS=1` to preserve the temp repo — a symlink appears in the artifact dir pointing to it.\n    66\t\n    67\tUse the `debug-e2e` skill (`.claude/skills/debug-e2e/`) for a structured workflow when investigating failures.\n    68\t\n    69\t### Reading artifacts\n    70\t\n    71\t- `console.log` — full operation transcript including agent stdout/stderr\n    72\t- `git-log.txt` — commit history at time of failure\n    73\t- `git-tree.txt` — working tree state\n    74\t- `entire-logs/` — internal CLI logs\n    75\t\n    76\t### Fixing flaky tests\n    77\t\n    78\tWhen a test passes on retry but failed once, the problem is usually agent non-determinism, not a CLI bug. Common patterns:\n    79\t\n    80\t- **Agent asked for confirmation instead of acting**: The model output contains \"Does this look right?\" or \"Should I proceed?\". Fix: append \"Do not ask for confirmation, just make the change.\" to the prompt.\n    81\t- **Agent wrote to wrong path or created extra files**: Fix: be more explicit about exact file paths and what _not_ to do.\n    82\t- **Agent committed when it shouldn't have**: Fix: add \"Do not commit\" to the prompt.\n    83\t- **Checkpoint wait timeout**: `WaitForCheckpoint` or `WaitForCheckpointAdvanceFrom` exceeded deadline. Fix: increase the timeout argument.\n    84\t\n    85\tTo diagnose: read `console.log` in the failing test's artifact directory. Compare what the agent actually did vs what the test expected.\n    86\t\n    87\t## CI Workflows\n    88\t\n    89\t- **`.github/workflows/e2e.yml`** — Runs full suite on push to main. Matrix: `[claude-code, opencode, gemini-cli, codex, cursor-cli, factoryai-droid, copilot-cli]`.\n    90\t- **`.github/workflows/e2e-isolated.yml`** — Manual dispatch for debugging a single test. Inputs: agent + test name filter.\n    91\t\n    92\tBoth workflows run `go run ./e2e/bootstrap` before tests to handle agent-specific CI setup (auth config, warmup).\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3625},"formatted_output":"","status":"completed"}}
